{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1004681-sanctum-sigil-how-useful-with-2e","id":1004681,"title":"Sanctum & Sigil how useful with 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T15:51:33-08:00","id":1004681,"title":"Sanctum & Sigil how useful with 2E?","content":"I've been away from the system for a while and just recently, last week, picked up 2E. I noticed the sanctum merit is different. How convertible is the 1E Sanctum &amp; Sigil to 2E? Is it worth using with 2E or is something new coming down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:43:20-08:00","id":1004703,"title":"","content":"Sanctum&amp;Sigil was mostly fluff about how cabals and consilii work, as such it's still compatible.<br /> <br /> Books after Core will be Signs of Sorcery and Tome of the Pentacle, so stuff from S&amp;S is unlikely to change or be updated any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T18:39:56-08:00","id":1004739,"title":"","content":"As Mrm said, it's mostly fluff so you're fine there.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've tweaked the Sanctum merit in my own games, though. Instead of adding to your Gnosis for spell control while inside it, the Sanctum dots provide one extra spell slot that you can store a spell in as you do for a Sleepwalker. The catch, of course, being that those spells must stay inside the Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T21:07:46-08:00","id":1004794,"title":"","content":"Well, some of the fluff about how cabals and consilii work has changed between editions (for cabals it mostly just amounts to &quot;mixed-Order cabals are now the rule rather than the exception&quot;, but the entire core role of the consilium is different in 2e, for one thing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T23:28:21-08:00","id":1004816,"title":"","content":"Mixed Order cabals were never the exception, they deliberately mixed them in order to keep the alliance of the Pentacle firmly cemented.<br /> <br /> The role of the Consilium isn't actually all that different either, they just did a better job of addressing how the Caucus works in relation to it, and emphasizing that the Consilium isn't the only form of authority in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T02:24:34-08:00","id":1004845,"title":"","content":"I would second Mrmdubois on consilia. 2e is meant to play down the executive role of the consilia as a mage government in favour of it being a court, but S&amp;S devotes most of it's text to that judicial role anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}